  "step_3": "The decision reason requires adjusting probabilities below 20% by +10 percentage points, then computing a weighted sum. However, in this case, no outcome has a probability below 20% (A: 20%, B: 25%), so no adjustment is made. Therefore, the reason is inapplicable. The individual did not consider any probability adjustments, nor did they mention weighting or recalculating probabilities. Their reasoning was based on a direct comparison of the base probabilities and prize amounts. Since the decision reason cannot even be applied to the problem (no probabilities <20%), and the individual did not engage with any adjustment mechanism, it is impossible that they used this reason. The individual’s justification does not reflect the rule of the reason, and the reason itself is not applicable here.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
